sequenceDiagram
  participant User
  participant App as App.jsx
  participant Ctrl as openCveDrawer.js
  participant Drawer as DetailDrawer.jsx
  participant APIjs as api.js
  participant MW as request_context middleware
  participant R as routers/cves.py
  participant DB as database.py
  participant Ext as feeds/enrichment

  User->>App: click CVECard
  App->>Ctrl: open(cve preview)
  Ctrl->>Drawer: setSelectedCVE + loading
  Ctrl->>APIjs: fetchCVE(id)
  APIjs->>MW: GET /api/cves/{id}
  MW->>MW: assign X-Request-ID
  MW->>R: get_cve
  R->>DB: read row + joins
  par on-demand enrich
    R->>Ext: Sploitus, GreyNoise, OTX, OSV, CIRCL
    Ext-->>R: merged fields
  end
  R-->>APIjs: full CVE object
  APIjs-->>Ctrl: CVE JSON
  Ctrl->>Drawer: setSelectedCVE(full) + clear loading

  par Parallel fetches on drawer open
    Drawer->>APIjs: GET /api/cves/{id}/sentences
    Drawer->>APIjs: GET /api/cves/{id}/epss-history
    Drawer->>APIjs: GET /api/cves/{id}/momentum
    Drawer->>APIjs: GET /api/cves/{id}/correlation
    Drawer->>APIjs: POST /api/cves/{id}/risk
  end

  opt User opens Related tab
    Drawer->>APIjs: GET /api/cves/{id}/related
  end

  opt User opens Detect tab
    Drawer->>APIjs: GET /api/cves/{id}/detection
  end

  Drawer->>User: tabs render as each response arrives

  Note over Ctrl,Drawer: On fetch failure (A3/A5):<br/>notifyApiError toast + blocking overlay or banner<br/>with API detail, ref link to ingest log, retry.
